Z||000000||8Ball||08-20-2001||08:34 AM||||Well my car is nearly back on the road.<BR>The 3.1 stroker kit is out as one of the pistons is damaged. But everything else is going good. It appears that this car has never had a single oil or transmission fliud change in it's life. The oil was slugde and the trannie fluid was as thin as water.<BR>But no metal shaveing in the trannie pan so that is good.<P>It appears my voltage regulater may be going out and I have no dash lights atm. No bigie.<BR>Still need to flush the engine out a couple more times cause of the sludge. And also need to lube the chassis and she will be on the road for a real test.<P>We also adjusted all the shift points on the auto trannie so it wil wind out the gears a lil.<BR>Hopeing to be driving soon.<P>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||08-20-2001||05:27 PM||||Glad you're making progress!  It's good you're taking the time to desludge and clean everything as you go.  Sometimes I get impatient because it takes me forever to clean stuff.  Seems the older the car, the more cleaning work it needs.  Especially if the previous owner didn't take care of it, as you say.<P>I bet the car feels good about it, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.     <P> ||||reg||6
